# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Runtime secrets — the ONLY place you type these by hand.
#
# ── What this file is for ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Terraform never writes a runtime secret: a secret in state is a secret in a
# storage account, readable by anything with state access (docs/BOOTSTRAP.md
# step 8). So the vault is created EMPTY and seeded afterwards, out of band.
#
# This file is the source. The path is:
#
#     .env  ──scripts/set-gh-secrets.sh──▶  GitHub environment secrets
#                                              (Sentinel-infra · production)
#                                                        │
#                                              ci_infra.yml "Seed vault"
#                                                        ▼
#                                                   Key Vault
#
# You fill this once. Every later destroy → apply re-seeds automatically, which
# is what makes tearing the estate down to zero cheap enough to actually do.
#
# ── Why GitHub ENVIRONMENT secrets, not repo secrets ─────────────────────────
# An environment secret is readable only by a job that declares
# `environment: production`. A pull request cannot declare it. That is the same
# boundary already protecting the deploy identity, so a hostile PR cannot
# exfiltrate these — by construction, not by a rule someone could misconfigure.
#
# ── Copy this to .env and fill it ────────────────────────────────────────────
#     cp .env.example .env
#     $EDITOR .env
#     bash scripts/set-gh-secrets.sh
#
# `.env` is gitignored (.gitignore:151). This file is committed and must stay
# free of real values. Keep your own copy of the filled values in a password
# manager — GitHub secrets are write-only, you cannot read them back.
#
# ── Blanks are fine ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave a key empty if you do not have it yet. The push script skips empties and
# the seed step warns rather than failing: a partially seeded vault is a VALID
# state (docs/BOOTSTRAP.md step 8). Fill it in later and re-run apply.
#
# ── Name mapping ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCREAMING_SNAKE here and in GitHub; kebab-case in Key Vault, because Key Vault
# secret names allow only alphanumerics and hyphens. The seed step lowercases
# and swaps underscores for hyphens, so the mapping is mechanical, not a table
# someone has to maintain:
#
#     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  ->  anthropic-api-key
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── LLM providers — deliberately NOT here ────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic and OpenAI both support workload identity federation, so the backend
# pod authenticates with its projected service-account token and there is no key
# to store. Decision: architecture/decisions.md, 2026-08-30 (sentinel-brain).
# Built in backend phase 7 — infra phase 6 has no pod to federate from.
#
# Left here commented, not deleted, for one case: if phase 7 needs a stopgap
# before federation lands, uncomment, fill, and the seed step picks it up. Do
# that knowingly — a key that outlives its stopgap is how the vault ends up back
# at seven entries.
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Datadog (the incident signal the whole pipeline reacts to) ───────────────
# API key  = ingest.  APP key = query. Both are needed; they are not the same.
DATADOG_API_KEY=
DATADOG_APP_KEY=

# ── Langfuse (agent tracing) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Teams (where an incident is announced) ───────────────────────────────────
TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ── GitHub dispatch (the bridge Function's GITHUB_TOKEN) ─────────────────────
# Fine-grained PAT: repository access Keshav0375/Sentinel ONLY, permission
# Contents: Read and write (what repository_dispatch requires), 90-day expiry.
# Named DISPATCH_PAT because GitHub forbids secret names starting with GITHUB_;
# the seed step maps it onto GITHUB_PAT, which lands in Key Vault as
# github-pat. Blank = Datadog alerts reach Event Grid and stop at the bridge.
DISPATCH_PAT=
